<!--Post: 149--><!--Time: 1086031880-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST149"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilahsue<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilahsue<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 31, 2004 - 12:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sandy...you have BTK letters?  WHOLE letters?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 149-->
<!--Post: 151--><!--Time: 1086044366-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST151"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 31, 2004 - 3:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m sure Sandy meant the textual reproductions of portions of BTK&#39;s letters that have been released. <BR> <BR>Back to the <i>America&#39;s Most Wanted</i> episode: It was obvious to me while watching it that the Wichita police offered nothing in the way of sharing/cooperation. Not that I&#39;m at all surprised, but that would explain any discrepancies that might have occured in the AMW reenactments. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 151-->
<!--Post: 152--><!--Time: 1086051046-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST152"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 31, 2004 - 5:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That is correct. Most are reproductions.I do have a copy of the first page of the 5/5/04 letter,at least that is what it says. Its about the chapters the btk would like for a book about himself. I will give what ever I have for Tom to look over.I also found a interesting sort of confession from a person who calls himself &#34;Bernie&#34;. He apologizes for the things he has done in the past &#40;tongue in cheek&#41;.Could be a fraud, who knows for sure? At the end of his apology he writes: You&#39;re an absolutely fantastic person,and you&#39;re going to make me very, very happy when I kill you. Thanks.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 152-->
<!--Post: 160--><!--Time: 1086255540-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST160"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Unsub<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Unsub<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, June 03, 2004 - 2:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My understanding is that AMW segments are filmed by independent producers. I think this guy was doing this one on spec. He may have cut Bright out due to time limits etc. I thought it was pretty wortless myself except for the phone call. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 160-->
