</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 11, 2004 - 11:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I also missed the show. &#40;Christmas shopping in downtown San Francisco -- a mad house!&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1781-->
<!--Post: 1788--><!--Time: 1102862680-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1788"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 12, 2004 - 6:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->On Kevin Bright&#39;s previous feedback, I thought that he stated that BTK had a cap pulled so low on his face that he could barely see his eyes. Last night on AMW, it was stated that the killer had on a ski mask. Did I misread some things? And again, he stated that he was darker complexioned with a moustache. <BR> <BR>I find it interesting that he would wear a mask at all unless he expected more than one person to be there. Part of the thrill appears to be letting the victim look at the last face they will ever see on earth. Of course, we only have feedback from one person. He clearly did not wear a mask with the Vian murder, as one child recognized him from a previous encounter. Memories resulting from severe trauma and fear situations can return sporadically and possibly become more accurate over years. That was the only info I caught that was different from the facts that I thought I knew. Going from fiddle to Blue Grass Music was an interesting leap. <BR> <BR>Did anyone notice the typewriter lettering on the pictures of his letters? Some much darker than others. He is using an old and well worn machine, probably a manual one. Maybe he repaired them at one time. That typewriter may be the best clue to date: the needle if they ever locate the haystack.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1788-->
<!--Post: 1791--><!--Time: 1102868212-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1791"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 12, 2004 - 8:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t know, &#34;TEARDROP&#34;, I think the typewriter he&#39;s using may not be the big clue you think it is. Here&#39;s why: He could just as easily throw it away &amp; replace it with another one for $5 from the Salvation Army. But then again, he might be using it as his &#34;special&#34; typwriter. It may be the same one he&#39;s used in past letters. Once they search his possesions, I&#39;m sure they&#39;ll find way more obvious clues &#34;tying him&#34; to these murders. Like victim photos, car keys, drivers&#39; licenses, etc... <BR> <BR>Also, in the Bright assault, brother Kevin is documented as saying that BLT wore a dark &#39;cap&#39; pulled down almost to his eyes. Not a &#34;ski mask&#34;. I don&#39;t remember him saying &#34;ski mask&#34; last night, but I could have missed something. It was pretty amazing to see Kevin so calm &amp; collected about it all. And with no obvious physical scars! Considering he was shot twice in the face at point-blank range, it&#39;s a miracle.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1791-->
<!--Post: 1797--><!--Time: 1102882650-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1797"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 12, 2004 - 12:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He did say ski mask and the recreation showed a man in camo wear and a ski mask. Eyewitness testimony can also be very unreliable at times because of the pace of the events and the emotion involved. The missfire is what was so surprising. And Kevin was calm, probably because he could not afford to be so  emotionally involved as to relive the events. A kind of dreamlike, movie theatre feeling. <BR> <BR>I still think that the typewriter is a good clue, if not from a physical standpoint &#40;until it is located&#41; as from a mind set and behavioral aspect. We return to familiar behaviors/things in time of stress, even if those behaviors did not serve us well in the past. They are still tried and true friends to some.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1797-->
</table></td></tr></table>
